// check: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// CROWN modal (§11 6.3's opening walk, measured 2026-08-08): the
// conjunction's other half — the SAME escaped closure performed under
// an outer !E must REFUSE: the install's subtraction applied at
// evaluation, the closure's row kept E riding the value, and the
// negation catches the escaped performance. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(1) }
fn make() = () => op()
fn escaped() = (make()) ~> h
fn outer() with !E = escaped()()
fn main() = outer()
